@* A section RCL does NOT inherit the host's Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Omitting a line
   here ships broken markup with a green build and no runtime error — see design §1/§2.
   Guarded by DevelopmentPageRenderTests (step 12). *@
@using Humans.Development
@using Humans.Development.Controllers
@using Humans.Development.Services
@using Humans.Base
@using Humans.Base.Models
@using Humans.Base.Models.Tables
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Html
@using System.Text.Encodings.Web
@* Development carries no resource set of its own — every string on the dev sign-in page and
   the user chooser is English developer copy, and there is no Development_* key anywhere
   (step 3b's opening question answers "no"). Unlike Debug, no type here binds a localizer at
   all, so DevelopmentArchitectureTests ships Gate's stricter guard: no IStringLocalizer<T>
   for any T. *@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@* A section can only addTagHelper against Humans.UI — a Shell-resident component renders
   as inert literal markup (step 6). *@
@addTagHelper *, Humans.Base
